# FEX on Aurora

This is FEX built from Aurora's fork (https://github.com/aurora-silicon/fex),
packaged under Fedora's fex-emu names so that it replaces Fedora's build:
`dnf install fex-emu` installs it. (Fedora's `fex` is an unrelated tool.)

## 4 KiB pages

FEX needs a 4 KiB page size. Aurora kernels use 16 KiB pages but can give a
process tree 4 KiB pages when the kernel is booted with `user4k=on` (the
default on Aurora images; `aurora-userpages` adds it on installed systems).
Start x86 programs inside a 4 KiB tree:

    userpages 4k FEXBash
    userpages 4k FEX ./program

Programs started from a 4 KiB tree inherit it, including x86 programs that
binfmt_misc hands to FEX. Started from an ordinary 16 KiB process,
FEX runs with 16 KiB pages and x86 programs fail. `userpages --status` shows
the current page size. Aurora's Steam launcher starts Steam in a 4 KiB tree.

## Hardware TSO

On kernels that offer the memory-model prctl (PR_SET_MEM_MODEL), FEX switches
the process to the hardware total store order mode and drops its software
TSO emulation. Check with:

    FEXGetConfig --tso-emulation-info

## x86 parity and adjust flags

Apple cores can compute the x86 parity and adjust flags, PF and AF, in
hardware. When the kernel advertises this extension, called APFLG, FEX turns
it on at startup and keeps PF and AF in the host flags instead of computing
them in software. `FEX_HOSTFEATURES=disableapflg` turns it off.

## Root filesystem

FEX needs an x86-64 root filesystem for anything but static programs. The
global config, /usr/share/fex-emu/Config.json, sets RootFS to
/usr/share/fex-emu/RootFS/default.erofs, the image from fex-emu-rootfs-fedora
(dnf installs it with fex-emu unless weak dependencies are turned off).
FEXServer mounts the image with erofsfuse when FEX starts, and runs
erofsfuse with native pages (a 4 KiB page process can't serve a FUSE mount on
Aurora's kernels), so `userpages 4k FEXBash` works without setup. To see the
mounted RootFS:

    userpages 4k FEXGetConfig --current-rootfs

If the image is missing, FEX's error names the package to install:

    sudo dnf install fex-emu-rootfs-fedora

Your own config, ~/.config/fex-emu/Config.json (~/.fex-emu/Config.json if
that directory exists), and the FEX_ROOTFS environment variable override the
global RootFS. A RootFS given as a name rather than a path is looked up in
~/.local/share/fex-emu/RootFS and /usr/share/fex-emu/RootFS.
`FEXRootFSFetcher` downloads other root filesystems and `FEXConfig` edits
your config. Both are in fex-emu-utils:

    sudo dnf install fex-emu-utils

Fedora Asahi Remix ran FEX in muvm, which set the RootFS only inside its VM.
On Aurora FEX runs on the host and uses the global config.

fex-emu also mounts the image at /usr/share/guestos/fex-mesa, the lower layer
of mesa-aurora-fex-guest's graphics provider, which Steam's FEX titles use
for the G17P Mesa (unless a provider tree is already there).
